Wrench dual-use disclosure

Wrench is a bring-your-own-agent command-line interface and TypeScript SDK for
authorized web capture, verified media archiving, encrypted cross-provider
reads, and typed provider operations.

Some Wrench capabilities can read a local browser profile or its cookies,
issue authenticated requests, automate a reviewed browser surface, and submit
provider writes after an exact preview and explicit confirmation. These
capabilities can expose private account data or change an external account if
they are used without the account holder's authorization.

Use Wrench only with accounts, data, and systems that you are authorized to
access. Review the selected provider, account realm, operation, inputs, and
preview before confirming a write. Preserve its durable receipts and treat an
indeterminate dispatch as unresolved rather than retrying it.

Wrench does not grant authorization, bypass login, payment, access controls, or
DRM, and does not turn source plugins into a hostile-code sandbox. Its intended
use is to give a user-selected agent a bounded, inspectable capability while
the user retains local custody of credentials and approval of consequential
actions.
